    {
      "id": "u0aSLYQi7xI0Y6XFpv4rt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1581.2658730158735,
      "y": 1842.9166666666665,
      "width": 854.5594482421875,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b10",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 900892605,
      "version": 1897,
      "versionNonce": 964954941,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788505374039,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Algorithms:\n\nLeaky Bucket: we keep a queue and store a constant number of request in that \nand keep taking constant req per second regardless. if the queue is full then we \nthrow 429.\nPROS: 1. Stable traffic control. 2. Easy to understand and implement.\nCONS: 1. Lacks flexibality in handling sudden traffic spikes.  \n\nUse Case: Network Bandwidth Management, Video Streaming etc.\n\nToken Bucket Algorithm: We keep a bucket for tokens and that has two properties,\nrate at which the bucket will fill with tokens ie. x/sec and capacity ie. y tokens.\nwhen a set of req come we only respond to the number of request we have tokens for\nif we don't have ant tokens then we throw 429.\nPROS: 1. Flexible in handling short term burst. 2. Easy to understand and implement.\nCONS: 1. Memory consumption at user level. 2. Lack of guarantee of smooth requests \nrate. 3. Complex parameter  tuning.\n\nUse Case: API rate limiting.\n\nFixed Window counter: we fix a time window and then only a fix amount of request are \nallowed in that window, the counter resets after that fixed interval for new requests.\nPROS: 1. Simple and easy to implement. 2. Allows burst of requests.\nCONS: 1.  Window boundary issue can exceed the request threshold by double.\n\nUse Case: if needed a simple rate limiter.\n\nSliding Window: Here we keep the window dynamic and moves with the latest request.\nwe keep a rate like 3/10sec, then if we get a request at 2sec,4sec,7sec then the \nrequest at 9sec will be rejected but when a req comes at   13th sec then we remove \nthe 2sec req. from our list and allow this new one.\nPROS: Fine grained traffic control\nCONS: Increased complexity.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Algorithms:\n\nLeaky Bucket: we keep a queue and store a constant number of request in that \nand keep taking constant req per second regardless. if the queue is full then we \nthrow 429.\nPROS: 1. Stable traffic control. 2. Easy to understand and implement.\nCONS: 1. Lacks flexibality in handling sudden traffic spikes.  \n\nUse Case: Network Bandwidth Management, Video Streaming etc.\n\nToken Bucket Algorithm: We keep a bucket for tokens and that has two properties,\nrate at which the bucket will fill with tokens ie. x/sec and capacity ie. y tokens.\nwhen a set of req come we only respond to the number of request we have tokens for\nif we don't have ant tokens then we throw 429.\nPROS: 1. Flexible in handling short term burst. 2. Easy to understand and implement.\nCONS: 1. Memory consumption at user level. 2. Lack of guarantee of smooth requests \nrate. 3. Complex parameter  tuning.\n\nUse Case: API rate limiting.\n\nFixed Window counter: we fix a time window and then only a fix amount of request are \nallowed in that window, the counter resets after that fixed interval for new requests.\nPROS: 1. Simple and easy to implement. 2. Allows burst of requests.\nCONS: 1.  Window boundary issue can exceed the request threshold by double.\n\nUse Case: if needed a simple rate limiter.\n\nSliding Window: Here we keep the window dynamic and moves with the latest request.\nwe keep a rate like 3/10sec, then if we get a request at 2sec,4sec,7sec then the \nrequest at 9sec will be rejected but when a req comes at   13th sec then we remove \nthe 2sec req. from our list and allow this new one.\nPROS: Fine grained traffic control\nCONS: Increased complexity.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
